# Plexa Database Migrations

This directory contains the Alembic environment and ordered PostgreSQL schema
migrations for Plexa. Migrations are the authoritative schema workflow; the
application must not create or reshape production tables at startup.

Run Alembic from the repository root so the project configuration and imports
resolve consistently:

```bash
uv run alembic -c plexa_server/alembic.ini upgrade head
uv run alembic -c plexa_server/alembic.ini current
uv run alembic -c plexa_server/alembic.ini history
```

Create a revision after updating the SQLAlchemy models:

```bash
uv run alembic -c plexa_server/alembic.ini revision --autogenerate -m "describe the schema change"
```

> [!CAUTION]
> Autogeneration is a draft, not a finished migration. Review upgrade and
> downgrade behavior, constraints, indexes, data backfills, and locking impact
> before committing the revision.

Migration files live in `versions/`. Keep revisions linear unless a deliberate
branch and merge migration has been reviewed. Test both clean-database upgrades
and upgrades from the previous release before deploying a schema change.

Production Compose runs `alembic upgrade head` in the one-shot `plexa_migrate`
service before the API starts. See [`../../deploy/README.md`](../../deploy/README.md)
for deployment, backup, and restore procedures.
